hadiths[69]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18568","It is reported from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said to Jibril, peace be upon him, asking why he never saw Mikail laughing. > **""Why is it that I never see Mikail laughing at all?""**"
"18569","It is reported from Yaʿla ibn Umayyah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ said that the sea is Hell. When people questioned Yaʿla about this, he cited the verse about the Fire whose walls surround its people, and he swore by the One in Whose Hand is his soul that he would never enter it until he is presented before Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and not a drop of it would touch him until he meets Allah. > **""The sea is Hell.""**"
"18570","Yazid ibn Abi Sawrah reports that he saw ʿUbadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, leaning his chest upon the wall of the mosque overlooking the Valley of Hell, weeping. When Yazid asked him, O father of al-Walid, what makes you weep, ʿUbadah replied that this was the place where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had seen Hell. > **""This is the place where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us that he saw Hell.""**"
"18571","ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmir al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that they prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he lengthened the standing, though he would usually shorten it, and they heard him saying, O my Lord, while I am among them. He then reached out his hand as if to grasp something, then bowed and hastened the remainder. After the greeting he sat and they sat around him, and he said he knew his long standing had troubled them. They confirmed they had heard him say, O my Lord, while I am among them. He swore by the One in Whose Hand is his soul that everything promised in the Hereafter had been shown to him, even the Fire, which advanced until it stood facing his place, so he feared it would envelop them and said, O my Lord, while I am among them, so Allah turned it away from them. It then came in pieces like heavy carpets, and he peered into it and saw in it ʿAmr ibn Hurthan, the brother of Banu Ghifar, fallen upon his bow in Hell, and the Himyari woman, the owner of the cat which she had tied without feeding or watering it nor letting it seek its food until it died. > **""O my Lord, while I am among them?""**"
"18572","It is reported from ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet ﷺ grieving, not raising his head. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him why he appeared grieved, and he replied that he had seen a blast of his spirit and it had not yet returned to him. > **""I saw a blast of Hellfire and my soul has not returned to me since.""**"
"18573","ʿUmar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that Jibril came to the Prophet ﷺ at an hour other than his usual hour. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to meet him and asked why his colour had changed. Jibril said he had not come until Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, commanded regarding the keys of the Fire. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him to describe the Fire and depict Hell. Jibril said Allah commanded Hell and it was stoked for a thousand years until it turned white, then for a thousand years until it turned red, then for a thousand years until it turned black, so it is black and dark, its sparks give no light and its flame is never extinguished. By the One Who sent him with the truth, if but the size of a needle's eye were opened from Hell, all on earth would die of its heat. By the One Who sent him with the truth, if a keeper of Hell appeared before the people of this world, all on earth would die from the ugliness of his face and the foulness of his odour. By the One Who sent him with the truth, if a single link of the chains of the people of the Fire described by Allah in His Book were placed upon the mountains of this world, they would crumble and not settle until reaching the lowest earth. > **""Describe the Fire for me and depict Hell for me.""**"
"18574","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that if a bucket of Hell were placed in the middle of the earth, the foulness of its odour and the severity of its heat would harm all between the east and the west, and if a single spark of Hell were in the east, its heat would be felt in the west. > **""If a bucket of Hell were placed in the middle of the earth, the foulness of its odour and the severity of its heat would harm all between the east and the west.""**"
"18575","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that this worldly fire is one part of a hundred parts of Hell. > **""This fire is one part of a hundred parts of Hell.""**"
"18576","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, asking whether they knew the likeness of their fire compared to the fire of Hell, that it is blacker than the smoke of their fire by seventy times. > **""Do you know the likeness of this fire of yours compared to the fire of Hell? It is blacker than the smoke of this fire of yours by seventy times over.""**"
"18577","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that he mentioned the fire of Hell and said it is one part of seventy parts of the fire of Hell, and it only reached them after it had been quenched twice with water so that it might give them light, while the fire of Hell is black and dark. > **""It is one part of seventy parts of the fire of Hell.""**"
"18578","ʿAbdullah ibn Masʿud, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that the righteous dream is glad tidings and is one part of seventy parts of prophethood, and that their fire is one part of seventy parts of the scorching heat of Hell, and that the servant remains in prayer so long as he waits for the prayer, provided he does not break his ablution. > **""Your fire, meaning this one, is one part of seventy parts of the scorching heat of Hell.""**"
"18579","Abu Saʿid, may Allah be pleased with him, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that the severity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell, so cool the prayer in severe heat, and that the Fire complained to its Lord, saying O my Lord, parts of me consume one another, so He permitted it two breaths each year, its breath in winter being the bitter cold and its breath in summer being the scorching heat. > **""The severity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell, so cool the prayer.""**"
"18580","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that the Fire complained to its Lord, saying O my Lord, parts of me consume one another, so He made for it two breaths, a breath in winter and a breath in summer, so the severity of the heat they feel is from its heat and the severity of the cold they feel is from its bitter cold. > **""My parts consume one another, so He made for it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer.""**"
"18581","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that Hell said, O my Lord, permit me to breathe, for I fear I shall seize upon Your creation, so He permitted it two breaths each year, twice, so the severity of heat is from its exhalation and the severity of cold is from its bitter cold. > **""O my Lord, permit me to breathe, for I fear I shall seize upon Your creation.""**"
"18582","ʿAbdullah ibn Masʿud, may Allah be pleased with him, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that Hell will be brought forth dragged by seventy thousand reins, with each rein seventy thousand angels pulling it. > **""Hell will be brought forth dragged by seventy thousand reins, with each rein seventy thousand angels pulling it.""**"
"18583","Abu Saʿid al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, reports from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning an iron mace of Hell, that were it placed upon the earth and both the jinn and mankind gathered to lift it, they could not move it from the earth. > **""If an iron mace were placed upon the earth and the two worlds gathered for it, they could not lift it from the earth.""**"
"18584","Abu Saʿid, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that if a mountain were struck with an iron mace of Hell, it would crumble to dust and then return as it was. > **""If a mountain were struck with an iron mace, it would crumble and then return.""**"
"18585","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded seeking refuge in Allah from Jubb al-Huzn. When asked what it is, he explained it is a valley in Hell from whose evil Hell itself seeks refuge with Allah four hundred times each day, into which the deceivers will be cast. When asked who the deceivers are, he said they are those who show off with their deeds in this world. > **""Seek refuge with Allah from Jubb al-Huzn, a valley in Hell into which the show-offs with their deeds will be cast.""**"
"18586","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that when the people of Hell are driven to it, Hell meets them and blasts them with a blast that leaves no flesh upon a bone but casts it down at the ankles. > **""When Hell is driven to its people, it meets them and blasts them with a blast that leaves no flesh upon a bone but casts it at the ankles.""**"
"18587","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that if a stone weighing as much as seven pregnant she-camels with their fat and offspring were cast into Hell, it would fall for seventy years and never reach its bottom. > **""If a stone of seven pregnant camels with their fat and offspring were cast into Hell, it would fall for seventy years and never reach its bottom.""**"
"18588","Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that if a stone were hurled into Hell, it would fall for seventy autumns before reaching its bottom. > **""If a stone were hurled into Hell, it would fall for seventy autumns before reaching its bottom.""**"
"18589","Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Prophet ﷺ said that if a stone were falling in Hell, it would not reach its bottom for seventy autumns. > **""If a stone were falling in Hell, it would not reach its bottom for seventy autumns.""**"
"18590","Abu Saʿid al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a terrifying sound, and Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him. The Prophet asked what the sound was, and Jibril said it was a boulder that fell from the edge of Hell seventy years ago and only now reached its bottom, and Allah loved that he should let him hear its sound. After that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never seen laughing with a full open mouth until Allah took him. > **""This is a boulder that fell from the edge of Hell seventy years ago, and only now has it reached its bottom.""**"
"18591","Luqman ibn ʿAmir reports that he came to Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him to narrate what he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Umamah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said that if a boulder weighing ten pregnant camels were hurled from the edge of Hell, it would not reach its bottom for seventy autumns until ending in Ghayy and Atham. When asked what they are, it was said they are two wells in Hell in which flows the pus of the people of the Fire, the same two mentioned by Allah in His Book regarding those who neglected prayer and followed desires meeting Ghayy, and whoever does that meeting Atham. > **""If a boulder weighing ten pregnant camels were hurled from the edge of Hell, it would not reach its bottom for seventy autumns until ending in Ghayy and Atham.""**"
"18592","From some people of knowledge, that Muʿadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ swore by the One in Whose Hand is his soul that the distance from the edge of the Fire to its bottom is such that a boulder weighing seven pregnant camels with their fat, flesh and offspring, falling therein, would take seventy autumns to reach its bottom. > **""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the distance from the edge of the Fire to its bottom is a boulder of seven pregnant camels falling for seventy autumns.""**"
"18593","ʿAbdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jazʾ al-Zubaydi, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that in the Fire are serpents like the necks of Bukht camels, one sting of which leaves its burning pain for seventy autumns, and in the Fire are scorpions like saddled mules, one sting of which leaves its burning pain for forty years. > **""In the Fire are serpents like the necks of Bukht camels, and in the Fire are scorpions like saddled mules.""**"
"18594","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that the lifespan of a fly is forty nights, and all flies are in the Fire except the bee. > **""All flies are in the Fire except the bee.""**"
"18595","Ibn ʿAbbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that all flies are in the Fire except the bee. > **""All flies are in the Fire except the bee.""**"
"18596","Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that all flies are in the Fire except the bee, and then the narrator mentioned the full hadith. > **""All flies are in the Fire except the bee.""**"
"18597","Ibn Masʿud, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that all flies are in the Fire except the bee. > **""All flies are in the Fire except the bee.""**"
"18598","Yaʿla ibn Munabbih, may Allah be pleased with him, raised the hadith to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will raise a black dark cloud for the people of the Fire. It will be said, O people of the Fire, what do you seek. They will recall the clouds of this world and say, O our Lord, drink. Then it will rain upon them fetters increasing their fetters, chains added to their chains, and embers blazing over them. > **""O people of the Fire, what do you seek?""**"
"18599","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that the sun and the moon are two lightless orbs cast in the Fire. > **""The sun and the moon are two lightless orbs in the Fire.""**"
"18600","ʿAbdullah ibn Masʿud, may Allah be pleased with him, said concerning the words of Allah, Exalted is He, We shall increase them in torment upon torment, that they will be given additional scorpions whose fangs are like tall palm trees. > **""They will be given additional scorpions whose fangs are like tall palm trees.""**"
"18601","Ibn ʿAbbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said concerning the words of Allah, Exalted is He, We shall increase them in torment upon torment, that they are five rivers beneath the Throne, punished by some of them by night and by some by day. > **""They are five rivers beneath the Throne, punished by some by night and by some by day.""**"
"18602","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that if there were a hundred or more in this mosque and a man of the Fire breathed therein and his breath touched them, the mosque and all in it would burn. > **""If there were a hundred in this mosque and a man of the Fire breathed and his breath touched them, the mosque and all in it would burn.""**"
"18603","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that if there were a hundred thousand or more in the mosque and then a man of the people of the Fire breathed, he would burn them all. > **""If there were a hundred thousand in the mosque and a man of the people of the Fire breathed, he would burn them all.""**"
"18604","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, O people, weep, and if you cannot weep then feign weeping, for the people of the Fire weep in the Fire until their tears flow upon their cheeks as though streams, until the tears cease and then blood flows, so the eyes become ulcerated, such that if ships were set afloat therein they would sail. > **""O people, weep, for if you cannot weep then feign weeping, for the people of the Fire weep in the Fire.""**"
"18605","Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that the people of the Fire will be magnified in the Fire, so that between the earlobe of one of them and his shoulder is a journey of seven hundred years, and the thickness of his skin is seventy cubits, and his skin is like Mount Uhud. > **""The people of the Fire will be magnified in the Fire until between the earlobe of one of them and his shoulder is seven hundred years.""**"
"18606","Abu Saʿid, may Allah be pleased with him, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that the seat of the disbeliever in the Fire is a journey of three days, every molar like Mount Uhud, his thigh like Mount Waraqan, and his skin apart from his flesh and bones forty cubits. > **""The seat of the disbeliever in the Fire is a journey of three days, every molar like Uhud.""**"
"18607","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that the molar of the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection will be like Mount Uhud, the width of his skin seventy cubits, and his seat in the Fire like the distance between Madinah and al-Rabadhah. > **""The molar of the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection will be like Uhud, and the width of his skin seventy cubits.""**"
"18608","Yazid ibn Hayyan al-Taymi reports that he, Husayn ibn Sabrah and ʿUmar ibn Muslim went to Zayd ibn Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, who narrated in that gathering that a man of the people of the Fire will be magnified for the Fire until a single molar of his is like Mount Uhud. > **""A man of the people of the Fire will be magnified for the Fire until a molar of his is like Uhud.""**"
"18609","Mujahid reports that Ibn al-ʿAbbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, asked whether he knew the vastness of Hell. When he said no, Ibn ʿAbbas said that between their earlobes and shoulders is seventy autumns, with valleys of pus flowing therefrom. When asked whether they were rivers, he said rather valleys, and then he mentioned the hadith. > **""Do you know the vastness of Hell? Between their earlobes and shoulders is seventy autumns.""**"
"18610","Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked and said that the molar of the disbeliever is like Mount Uhud, and the thickness of his skin forty cubits by the cubit of al-Jabbar. > **""The molar of the disbeliever is like Uhud, and the thickness of his skin forty cubits by the cubit of al-Jabbar.""**"
"18611","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that the first to be clothed with a garment of the Fire is Iblis, who will place it upon his eyebrow and drag it after him while his offspring follow behind him, he crying O my destruction and they crying O their destruction twice, until they stand over the Fire, whereupon he says O my destruction and they say O their destruction, and it will be said to them, call not this day for one destruction but call for many destructions. > **""The first to be clothed with a garment of the Fire is Iblis, who will place it upon his eyebrow and drag it after him.""**"
"18612","Abu Saʿid, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying that when Allah gathers mankind in one plain on the Day of Resurrection, the Fire will advance with parts riding upon parts, its keepers holding it back, while it says, by the might of my Lord, either leave me with my spouses or I shall envelop mankind all at once. They will say, who are your spouses. It will say, every arrogant tyrant, then it will extend its tongue and snatch them from among the people and hurl them into its belly, then withdraw. Then it will advance again with parts riding upon parts while its keepers hold it back, saying, by the might of my Lord, either leave me with my spouses or I shall envelop mankind all at once. They will say, who are your spouses. It will say, every tyrannical disbeliever, and snatch them with its tongue and hurl them into its belly, then withdraw. Then it will advance a third time saying likewise, and they will ask who its spouses are, and it will say, every tyrannical boaster, snatching them with its tongue and hurling them into its belly, then withdraw, and Allah will judge between the servants. > **""By the might of my Lord, either leave me with my spouses or I shall envelop mankind all at once.""**"
"18613","Abu Saʿid, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that a neck will emerge from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, speaking with an eloquent fluent tongue, having two eyes with which it sees and a tongue with which it speaks, saying it has been commanded to seize whoever ascribed another god with Allah, every obstinate tyrant, and whoever killed a soul without right, then it will carry them off five hundred years before the rest of mankind. > **""I have been commanded to seize whoever ascribed another god with Allah, every obstinate tyrant, and whoever killed a soul without right.""**"
"18614","In another narration, it will fold over them and hurl them into Hell. > **""It will fold over them and hurl them into Hell.""**"
"18615","Muhammad ibn Wasiʿ reports that he said to Bilal ibn Abi Burdah that his father narrated from his grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that in Hell is a valley, and in the valley a well called Habhab, and it is binding upon Allah to lodge therein every obstinate tyrant. > **""In Hell is a valley, and in the valley a well called Habhab, and it is binding upon Allah to lodge therein every obstinate tyrant.""**"
"18616","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, asking whether he should inform them of the people of the Fire: every foolish, coarse person. > **""Shall I not inform you of the people of the Fire? Every foolish coarse person.""**"
"18617","ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAs, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said at the mention of the Fire that the people of the Fire are every coarse, swaggering, arrogant hoarder and withholder, while the people of Paradise are the weak and overpowered. > **""The people of the Fire are every coarse, swaggering, arrogant hoarder and withholder, while the people of Paradise are the weak and overpowered.""**"
"18618","Ibn Ghunm reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that the swaggering coarse one and the cruel ill-born shall not enter Paradise. > **""The swaggering coarse one and the cruel ill-born shall not enter Paradise.""**"
"18619","ʿUlayy ibn Rabah reports that it reached him from Suraqah ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ said to him, O Suraqah, shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire. He said, yes, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet said, as for the people of the Fire, every coarse, swaggering, arrogant one, and as for the people of Paradise, the weak and overpowered. > **""O Suraqah, shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire?""**"
"18620","Ibn ʿAbbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying that Allah never sent a prophet to a people and took him but made after him an interval, and from that interval He fills Hell. > **""Allah never sent a prophet to a people and took him but made after him an interval, and from that interval He fills Hell.""**"
"18621","Abu al-Dardaʾ, may Allah be pleased with him, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say on the Day of Resurrection to Adam, peace be upon him, rise and dispatch of your offspring nine hundred and ninety nine to the Fire and one to Paradise. His Companions wept, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told them to raise their heads, swearing by the One in Whose Hand is his soul that his nation among the nations is but like a white hair upon the hide of a black bull, and that lightened it for them. > **""Rise and dispatch of your offspring nine hundred and ninety nine to the Fire and one to Paradise.""**"
"18622","ʿAbdullah ibn Masʿud, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will send a caller proclaiming, O Adam, Allah commands you to dispatch a contingent of your offspring to the Fire. Adam will say, O my Lord, how many. It will be said to him, of every hundred, ninety nine. A man among the people asked, who among us shall be saved after this, O Messenger of Allah. He asked whether they knew that they among mankind are but like a mole upon the chest of a camel. > **""Of every hundred, ninety nine to the Fire.""**"
"18623","Ibn ʿAbbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse while his Companions were with him, O mankind, fear your Lord, indeed the convulsion of the Hour is a tremendous thing, to the end of the verse, then asked whether they knew which day that is. They said Allah and His Messenger know best. He said it is the day Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says, O Adam, rise and dispatch a contingent to the Fire. Adam asks, what is the contingent of the Fire. He says, of every thousand, nine hundred and ninety nine to the Fire and one to Paradise. That weighed heavily upon the people, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said he hoped they would be a quarter of the people of Paradise, then a third of the people of Paradise, then half of the people of Paradise, then said work and receive glad tidings, for they are between two creations that never accompany anyone but multiply him, Gog and Magog, and they among mankind are but like a mole upon the side of a camel or a mark upon the foreleg of a beast, his nation being but one part of a thousand parts. > **""Of every thousand, nine hundred and ninety nine to the Fire and one to Paradise.""**"
"18624","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the verse, O mankind, fear your Lord, up to His saying, the punishment of Allah is severe, was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ while on a journey, and he raised his voice with it until his Companions gathered to him. He asked whether they knew which day this is, the day Allah says to Adam, rise and dispatch a contingent to the Fire, of every thousand nine hundred and ninety nine to the Fire and one to Paradise. That weighed heavily upon the Muslims, so the Prophet ﷺ said be upright, draw near and receive glad tidings, swearing by the One in Whose Hand is his soul that they among mankind are but like a mole upon the side of a camel or a mark upon the foreleg of a beast, and with them are two creations that never accompany anything but multiply it, Gog and Magog and those perished among the disbelievers of jinn and men. > **""Of every thousand, nine hundred and ninety nine to the Fire and one to Paradise.""**"
"18625","ʿAbd al-Rahman ibn Shibl, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that the wicked are the people of the Fire. When asked who the wicked are, he said, women. A man asked, O Messenger of Allah, are they not our mothers and sisters and wives and daughters. He said yes, but when they are given they are not grateful, and when they are tried they are not patient. > **""The wicked are the people of the Fire.""**"
"18626","Hakim ibn Hizam, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded women to give charity and urged them to it, saying give charity for you are most of the people of the Fire. A woman among them asked why, O Messenger of Allah. He said because they curse frequently, delay good, and deny their husbands. > **""Give charity, for you are most of the people of the Fire.""**"
"18627","Ibn ʿAbbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that none enters the gate of the Fire but one who quenches his anger through the displeasure of Allah. > **""None enters the gate of the Fire but one who quenches his anger through the displeasure of Allah.""**"
"18628","Abu Saʿid, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that the lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment is a man wearing two sandals of fire from which his brain boils along with the rest of the punishment, and among them is one in the Fire up to his chest with the rest of the punishment, and among them one in the Fire up to his collarbone with the rest of the punishment, and among them one submerged therein. > **""The lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment is a man wearing two sandals of fire from which his brain boils.""**"
"18629","Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked whether he benefited Abu Talib in anything, and he said he brought him out of the Fire to its shallows. > **""I brought him out of the Fire to its shallows.""**"
"18630","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that the least of the people of the Fire in punishment is he who has two sandals of fire from which his brain boils. > **""The least of the people of the Fire in punishment is he who has two sandals of fire from which his brain boils.""**"
"18631","ʿImran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that whoever kills himself with a thing in this world will be punished with it in the Hereafter. > **""Whoever kills himself with a thing in this world will be punished with it in the Hereafter.""**"
"18632","Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that he swore by Allah that none leaves the Fire until he remains therein for ages, and an age is somewhat more than eighty years, each year three hundred and sixty days by their reckoning. > **""By Allah, none leaves the Fire until he remains therein for ages.""**"
"18633","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection like a black and white ram and stood between Paradise and the Fire, then a caller will call, O people of Paradise, and they will say, at Your service our Lord. It will be said, do you recognise this. They will say, yes our Lord, this is death, then it will be slaughtered as a sheep is slaughtered, so these will be secure and the hope of those will be cut off. > **""Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection like a black and white ram and slaughtered as a sheep is slaughtered.""**"
"18634","Muʿadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to Yemen, and when he arrived he said, O people, I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you, informing you that the return is to Allah, to Paradise or to Fire, an eternity without death and a residence without departure, in bodies that do not die. > **""The return is to Allah, to Paradise or to Fire, an eternity without death and a residence without departure.""**"
"18635","ʿAbdullah, meaning Ibn Masʿud, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that if it were said to the people of the Fire that they would remain therein for the number of every pebble in this world, they would rejoice at it, and if it were said to the people of Paradise that they would remain therein for the number of every pebble, they would grieve, but He has made for them eternity. > **""If it were said to the people of the Fire that they would remain for the number of every pebble, they would rejoice, but He has made for them eternity.""**"
"18636","ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reports that the people of the Fire will call upon Malik and he will not answer them for forty years, then he will say, indeed you shall remain. Then they will call upon their Lord saying, our Lord, bring us out of it, and if we return then we are wrongdoers, and He will not answer them for the like of this world, then He will say, remain despised therein and speak not to Me. Then the people will despair, and there will be nothing but sighing and gasping, their voices resembling the voices of donkeys, its beginning a gasp and its end a sigh. > **""Remain despised therein and speak not to Me.""**"
